# dubu-updater — local secrets template.
#
# Copy to `.env` NEXT TO THIS FILE and fill in the blanks. `.env` is gitignored at every depth
# by the repository root `.gitignore`; `.env.example` is the only one that is committed, and it
# must never hold a real value.
#
# Loading rules (see `config::load_dotenv`):
#   * `./.env` is read first, then `<directory of --config>/.env`.
#   * A variable already present in the real environment ALWAYS wins. The file is a convenience
#     for local runs, never an override of what an operator or a systemd unit set deliberately.
#   * Nothing read from here is ever logged. Endpoint URLs are wrapped in `config::EndpointUrl`,
#     whose `Display`/`Debug` are redacted, so the key cannot reach a log line by accident.

# --- Chain endpoints ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Nodit dedicated endpoint for GIWA Sepolia. The API key is the last path segment of the URL,
# which is why the whole URL is treated as a secret and redacted to `https://host/***` in logs.
#
# Get one at https://nodit.io — the free tier is enough for `eth_subscribe`, `eth_call`,
# `eth_blockNumber` and `eth_sendRawTransaction`. `debug_traceTransaction` needs a higher tier
# and `trace_block` does not exist on this chain; nothing in this crate calls either.
NODIT_API_KEY=

# --- Signing key -------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Only needed to broadcast. A dry run works with no key material present at all, which is most
# of what makes it safe to hand to someone. Must be the address `PropPool.updater()` returns —
# startup refuses to transmit as anyone else.
DUBU_UPDATER_KEY=
